WEBVTT

00:41.333 --> 00:43.961
NO TAIL TO TELL

00:45.128 --> 00:46.672
Maybe it's because I'm human now,

00:46.755 --> 00:50.050
but my heart keeps racing
for no reason whenever I look at you.

00:50.147 --> 00:53.470
I guess this is what
humans call romantic feelings.

00:53.554 --> 00:54.555
What?

00:56.223 --> 00:57.224
Si-yeol,

00:58.016 --> 00:59.393
I think

01:00.644 --> 01:01.895
I need to date you.

01:09.152 --> 01:10.571
Wait, hold on.

01:11.154 --> 01:13.740
Do you even know
what you're saying right now?

01:13.824 --> 01:17.452
Well, you're not bad-looking,

01:18.120 --> 01:20.789
and I'm not embarrassed
to be seen with you.

01:20.872 --> 01:23.375
- By the way, which Kang clan are you from?
- What?

01:23.458 --> 01:26.461
Don't you know your clan branch
and generation?

01:27.838 --> 01:30.132
You are from a noble lineage, right?

01:30.215 --> 01:32.801
Did any of your ancestors
hold an official post?

01:32.884 --> 01:36.179
Seriously, what are you talking about?

01:36.263 --> 01:37.472
As I told you before,

01:37.556 --> 01:39.891
I've tried everything
that looked even remotely fun

01:39.975 --> 01:41.977
while living in the human world.

01:42.603 --> 01:44.187
Except for one thing.

01:44.271 --> 01:46.690
- And you're saying that's--
- Yes, dating.

01:46.773 --> 01:51.069
I avoided dating, just in case
it made me want to become human.

01:51.153 --> 01:54.906
So I've gone out of my way
to avoid men all these years.

01:56.199 --> 01:57.951
But I don't need to do that now.

01:58.035 --> 02:01.455
I might as well try dating you
since I'm already human

02:01.538 --> 02:03.248
until I turn back to normal.

02:03.332 --> 02:04.833
So, Si-yeol.

02:05.542 --> 02:06.627
Go out with me.

02:08.712 --> 02:12.382
Are you making a move on me right now?

02:12.466 --> 02:14.092
No, this is an order.

02:14.176 --> 02:17.262
Cooperate if you want to go back
to your normal life.

02:21.933 --> 02:23.310
Do you like me?

02:24.519 --> 02:25.854
Are you insane?

02:25.937 --> 02:28.398
How dare a mere human think such a thing?

02:29.274 --> 02:30.859
It's just that

02:30.942 --> 02:33.945
you're qualified enough
and not embarrassing to be with.

02:34.029 --> 02:35.739
That's about it.

02:36.615 --> 02:38.617
Besides, it's not like
you'd dare reject me,

02:38.700 --> 02:40.619
so there's no problem, right?

02:40.702 --> 02:43.538
Why wouldn't there be a problem?

02:43.622 --> 02:46.750
No one starts a relationship like this,
not when you don't even like me.

02:46.833 --> 02:49.503
What's the big deal?

02:49.586 --> 02:53.840
It's not like all humans date
because they're madly in love.

02:53.924 --> 02:57.177
We'll be back to normal soon anyway,
so it's not like we'll be dating for long.

02:57.260 --> 03:01.431
Jeez, stop arguing with me
and just cooperate.

03:02.849 --> 03:05.852
I'm actually pretty excited
about this new hobby.

03:07.270 --> 03:08.730
Hope we get along, honey.

03:19.324 --> 03:22.244
EPISODE 8
THE HOBBY CALLED LOVE

03:50.147 --> 03:51.606
What are you…

03:52.399 --> 03:53.734
Why are you here?

03:53.817 --> 03:55.485
What's with you?

03:55.569 --> 03:56.862
Did you sleep well, baby?

03:57.529 --> 04:00.907
Seriously, what's wrong with you?
It's way too early for this.

04:01.700 --> 04:03.368
Just act normal.

04:10.083 --> 04:13.086
What do you want now?

04:13.587 --> 04:15.630
Come here. Let me lie on your arm.

04:15.714 --> 04:18.592
Who told you to get up already?
Way to kill the mood.

04:24.556 --> 04:25.515
My neck hurts.

04:27.392 --> 04:28.435
Muscle cramp.

04:41.072 --> 04:42.282
What are you doing?

04:45.702 --> 04:47.996
Fine, whatever.

04:48.079 --> 04:49.164
I give up.

04:49.247 --> 04:50.457
Here.

04:59.800 --> 05:01.301
What now?

05:04.429 --> 05:06.014
Read the room.

05:09.059 --> 05:10.519
Open wide.

05:11.269 --> 05:12.521
Me?

05:13.730 --> 05:14.981
Open up.

05:21.196 --> 05:23.824
Does it taste different
when I feed it to you?

05:24.449 --> 05:27.452
It's still just a rolled omelet.
Why would it taste different?

05:27.536 --> 05:28.495
Really?

05:29.246 --> 05:32.415
But shouldn't it be different
when you're in a relationship?

05:33.458 --> 05:34.793
Actually, same here.

05:34.876 --> 05:37.587
Whether you feed me or not,
it tastes exactly the same.

05:38.964 --> 05:40.882
What am I doing wrong?

05:40.966 --> 05:44.302
That's why I'm telling you
to stop with all this.

05:44.928 --> 05:47.556
Why would I stop? We just started.

05:51.226 --> 05:52.519
Should we try holding hands?

05:56.773 --> 05:58.859
Hold my hand and I'll give you some water.

05:58.942 --> 06:00.318
What?

06:00.402 --> 06:01.319
Come on.

06:05.657 --> 06:06.992
Jeez.

06:08.618 --> 06:09.703
Here, drink.

06:15.500 --> 06:16.877
Seriously.

06:16.960 --> 06:18.879
Si-yeol, how about a date today?

06:20.005 --> 06:21.006
What?

06:21.590 --> 06:23.758
Let's go on a date
after we're done for the day.

06:23.842 --> 06:26.094
Isn't that what all couples do?

06:45.155 --> 06:46.573
Give me a break.

06:47.282 --> 06:49.618
Stop obsessing over this "couple" thing.

06:49.701 --> 06:51.828
What, is your hand that precious?

06:52.787 --> 06:55.165
It's not like
it'll wear out if I touch it.

06:55.248 --> 06:57.167
It'll rot away when you're dead anyway.

06:58.376 --> 06:59.628
So,

07:00.503 --> 07:02.255
what do you mean, "done for the day"?

07:03.214 --> 07:06.009
Are we volunteering
at the nursing home again today?

07:06.676 --> 07:07.761
Yes.

07:07.844 --> 07:11.640
Good deeds don't show results
overnight, you know.

07:11.723 --> 07:15.018
You have to do it for at least a week
to see if it actually works.

07:17.437 --> 07:20.607
Plus, there's something else
I want to look into while I'm there.

07:21.983 --> 07:23.068
Look into what?

07:24.277 --> 07:25.779
What happened yesterday.

07:27.113 --> 07:29.407
I've been trying to remember,

07:30.408 --> 07:32.661
but I have no idea who that old man is.

07:34.412 --> 07:37.582
Judging by his reaction,
he seems to have been a client of mine.

07:39.542 --> 07:43.964
But I don't get why he'd hold
such a grudge against me,

07:44.047 --> 07:47.801
which just really rubs me the wrong way.

07:50.720 --> 07:53.181
But how would you even find that out now?

07:53.765 --> 07:58.019
His memory seemed pretty shot to me.

07:58.853 --> 08:00.522
Well, he clearly remembers something.

08:00.605 --> 08:03.066
Otherwise, he wouldn't have
reacted that way.

08:03.149 --> 08:06.069
If I go ask him,
maybe I'll get something out of him.

08:13.827 --> 08:15.495
My grandmother is unbelievable.

08:15.578 --> 08:18.206
I'm here to visit, and she leaves
to hang out somewhere else?

08:18.289 --> 08:20.625
I'm the only one who always misses her.

08:20.709 --> 08:22.335
Well, of course.

08:22.419 --> 08:24.170
She probably saw you every day.

08:24.671 --> 08:28.216
Stop whining
and pull the sheet tight on your end.

08:28.299 --> 08:31.261
Jeez, the work is never-ending.

08:31.344 --> 08:34.055
Why are there so many beds?

08:34.139 --> 08:35.682
We're almost done.

08:36.516 --> 08:38.435
This is the last room.

08:38.518 --> 08:40.395
What? Already?

08:41.438 --> 08:42.939
What's with that reaction?

08:43.023 --> 08:46.067
I told you I had to ask
that old man something.

08:46.735 --> 08:48.486
But why isn't his room here?

08:49.112 --> 08:50.071
Hey.

08:50.655 --> 08:51.865
You're right.

08:54.826 --> 08:56.661
VOLUNTEER CLEANING CHECKLIST

08:56.745 --> 08:58.955
His name isn't even on the list.

08:59.831 --> 09:01.249
You there.

09:01.332 --> 09:02.667
Yes?

09:02.751 --> 09:05.670
Do you know where Mr. Hwang Dong-sik is?

09:07.589 --> 09:10.258
Mr. Hwang Dong-sik passed away last night.

09:12.510 --> 09:13.428
Pardon?

09:14.179 --> 09:15.305
He passed away.

10:40.515 --> 10:43.685
FUNERAL HALL

11:10.044 --> 11:12.213
REST IN PEACE

11:15.133 --> 11:16.593
Please, have a seat here.

11:16.676 --> 11:17.802
Thank you.

11:21.222 --> 11:24.184
What brings you all the way here?

11:24.726 --> 11:25.935
Well…

11:27.187 --> 11:29.355
We went to the nursing home earlier

11:29.439 --> 11:33.067
and heard the news about his passing.

11:34.319 --> 11:35.862
I had something to ask.

11:37.947 --> 11:40.074
- To me?
- That's right.

11:40.658 --> 11:43.119
I was going to ask him directly.

11:45.205 --> 11:47.040
But since that's no longer an option,

11:47.123 --> 11:49.292
I'll just have to ask you instead.

11:50.460 --> 11:52.045
I'm not sure…

11:52.128 --> 11:53.671
Please, help yourselves.

11:59.302 --> 12:00.929
- Honey, sit here.
- Okay.

12:06.392 --> 12:10.772
So, did you know my father-in-law?

12:11.898 --> 12:13.358
I'm trying to find that out.

12:16.861 --> 12:19.948
Oh, by the way…

12:20.031 --> 12:23.076
just so you know, she grew up abroad.

12:23.159 --> 12:26.204
So she hasn't learned
how to speak formally yet.

12:26.287 --> 12:28.164
What are you talking about?

12:28.248 --> 12:30.083
Look, pick one.

12:30.750 --> 12:33.586
Either speak politely
or just play along with what I'm saying.

12:33.670 --> 12:36.005
Stop making things awkward.

12:36.089 --> 12:37.465
Play along with what?

12:41.594 --> 12:42.637
Fine. Whatever.

12:44.389 --> 12:45.723
I'm actually

12:45.807 --> 12:47.684
from the City of Angels.

12:49.227 --> 12:50.687
City of Angels?

12:51.271 --> 12:52.772
It's a city in America.

12:54.023 --> 12:57.360
I think they call it Los Angeles now.

12:58.778 --> 13:02.407
Gosh, I'm not sure
where she's going with this.

13:04.117 --> 13:05.994
Why is this funeral so shabby?

13:06.703 --> 13:08.454
Didn't your family used to be well-off?

13:10.331 --> 13:12.375
Wait, how would you know that?

13:12.458 --> 13:14.711
Because he was my client.

13:15.586 --> 13:16.546
Pardon?

13:17.255 --> 13:20.425
They say wealth lasts
three generations even if you go broke.

13:20.508 --> 13:22.802
Why are you living like this?

13:22.885 --> 13:24.220
It's making me uncomfortable.

13:25.346 --> 13:26.681
Well-off? Yeah, right.

13:27.807 --> 13:29.017
When I married into his family,

13:29.100 --> 13:31.853
they were so poor that they didn't have
a matching set of anything.

13:31.936 --> 13:33.688
I wasn't lying about our wealth.

13:34.355 --> 13:35.606
I'm serious.

13:35.690 --> 13:37.317
When I was a kid,

13:37.400 --> 13:40.945
we had a chauffeur and lived
in a two-story house with a yard.

13:41.029 --> 13:43.531
Sure. Whatever you say.

13:44.157 --> 13:46.743
I wonder what happened to all that wealth.

13:46.826 --> 13:48.995
I'd sure love to see it for myself.

13:49.078 --> 13:50.830
Well, my father…

13:51.372 --> 13:53.875
Forget it. What's the point anyway?

13:57.587 --> 13:59.714
Don't just stop all of a sudden.

13:59.797 --> 14:01.883
Go on. I'm curious.

14:02.467 --> 14:04.177
Tell me about your father.

14:06.346 --> 14:08.014
You want us to sell you our new drug?

14:08.097 --> 14:10.016
THIRTY YEARS AGO
WORLD PHARMACEUTICAL

14:10.099 --> 14:10.975
I'm sorry, I can't.

14:11.601 --> 14:15.605
Even if you doubled your previous offer,
I would never--

14:16.105 --> 14:17.398
Ten times.

14:19.067 --> 14:20.318
Excuse me?

14:20.401 --> 14:21.486
Not double.

14:23.279 --> 14:24.405
I'm offering ten times more.

14:25.990 --> 14:28.368
Think it over carefully, Mr. Hwang.

14:31.954 --> 14:33.498
When it comes to new drugs,

14:34.123 --> 14:36.542
they're worthless
if they fail the clinical trials.

14:39.629 --> 14:40.838
Isn't it better…

14:42.882 --> 14:48.221
for you to take this money
and walk away, Mr. Hwang?

14:48.304 --> 14:51.224
Doesn't your company lack the funds

14:51.307 --> 14:53.726
to get through
Phase 3 of US clinical trials?

14:55.603 --> 14:57.980
Sell that drug to me.

15:01.734 --> 15:04.153
What a waste!

15:04.779 --> 15:07.073
He should've sold it back then.

15:07.156 --> 15:08.491
What do you mean?

15:08.574 --> 15:11.285
I mean, he held on to that drug
instead of selling it

15:11.369 --> 15:13.079
and ended up failing, didn't he?

15:13.162 --> 15:15.832
That has to be
why our family ended up like this.

15:16.457 --> 15:18.167
He sold it for ten times the price.

15:19.252 --> 15:20.878
How much was it again?

15:20.962 --> 15:23.339
Well, in today's money,

15:23.965 --> 15:26.926
it was enough
to buy a building in Gangnam.

15:27.009 --> 15:28.428
Really?

15:29.220 --> 15:30.721
Then where did all that money go?

15:31.514 --> 15:32.515
He lost it all.

15:33.141 --> 15:34.559
All of it?

15:34.642 --> 15:38.938
Was he scammed or something?
Or did he gamble it away?

15:39.021 --> 15:41.232
No, it wasn't anything like that.

15:41.315 --> 15:46.154
Apparently, those clinical trials ended up
being a huge success a few years later.

15:47.196 --> 15:48.531
But that was the problem.

15:49.157 --> 15:50.783
Why was that…

15:51.409 --> 15:52.660
My mother said…

15:54.662 --> 15:57.915
that my father became a bit strange.

15:59.083 --> 16:00.334
Like a man possessed.

16:00.418 --> 16:05.173
He wanted to make a new drug
that was even better than the one he sold.

16:05.798 --> 16:09.010
He poured money into a hopeless project

16:09.093 --> 16:10.887
and got into debt.

16:10.970 --> 16:13.139
He lost both the company and the house.

16:14.056 --> 16:16.726
But his entire life,
he'd never talk about it.

16:16.809 --> 16:19.395
I don't know the full story myself,

16:19.937 --> 16:25.276
but selling that drug like that
must've haunted him for life.

16:28.613 --> 16:30.990
Excuse me, I'm sorry to interrupt.

16:31.574 --> 16:34.785
Sir, as the chief mourner,
you need to select a coffin.

16:35.328 --> 16:36.621
Here are the different types--

16:36.704 --> 16:40.917
We'll take the cheapest one, please.

16:41.000 --> 16:44.378
- Our finances are a bit tight.
- I understand.

16:52.136 --> 16:53.262
So,

16:53.846 --> 16:55.681
did anything come to mind?

16:55.765 --> 16:56.933
Yes.

16:57.475 --> 16:59.769
That old man wasn't my client.

17:00.269 --> 17:01.395
Really?

17:02.063 --> 17:04.482
Actually, hearing the story,

17:04.565 --> 17:07.193
it didn't sound like his life
went south because of you.

17:07.276 --> 17:08.236
No.

17:08.736 --> 17:10.655
It was because of me.

17:11.405 --> 17:12.406
What?

17:14.700 --> 17:17.078
Si-yeol, go to that ATM
and withdraw some cash.

17:17.703 --> 17:19.455
Let's leave some condolence money.

17:19.539 --> 17:20.957
Sure.

17:22.291 --> 17:23.334
How much?

17:24.669 --> 17:26.420
We don't have much money left.

17:27.046 --> 17:28.548
Would 50,000 won be enough?

17:29.340 --> 17:31.801
Don't be cheap. Take everything out.

17:31.884 --> 17:33.636
You said it's not even that much anyway.

17:33.719 --> 17:36.847
Then what are we going to live on?

17:36.931 --> 17:39.600
It makes no difference. Just give it.

17:41.102 --> 17:44.564
You seem to have no idea
how scary being broke can be.

17:45.106 --> 17:48.234
How can anyone live without a single…

17:51.404 --> 17:54.031
Okay, whatever.

17:54.115 --> 17:55.533
We'll figure it out somehow.

17:56.742 --> 17:58.244
And if possible…

18:01.497 --> 18:03.916
tell them to use that money
to get the best coffin.

18:22.101 --> 18:23.436
Sis!

18:24.645 --> 18:26.022
What did you just do?

18:27.023 --> 18:28.190
What do you mean?

18:28.274 --> 18:29.942
I was just standing here.

18:30.526 --> 18:32.820
Why are you making such a fuss?

18:32.903 --> 18:35.740
I just gained spiritual power.

18:37.033 --> 18:37.908
What?

18:37.992 --> 18:42.079
It was a tiny, microscopic,
practically invisible amount,

18:42.163 --> 18:45.666
but I thought I should tell you
since it was still a gain.

18:45.750 --> 18:48.544
You tried doing good deeds for days,

18:48.628 --> 18:51.589
but no power was building up,
so I thought I was being scammed.

18:51.672 --> 18:53.549
You gained spiritual power?

18:54.050 --> 18:55.343
Just now?

18:56.677 --> 18:57.845
Hey.

18:57.928 --> 18:59.138
When did you get here?

19:00.598 --> 19:02.516
I just gave them the condolence money.

19:03.267 --> 19:07.021
It took a while
because they were refusing to take it.

19:10.191 --> 19:11.651
Anyway, what's going on?

19:11.734 --> 19:12.985
Si-yeol.

19:13.611 --> 19:14.987
I think I finally know

19:16.614 --> 19:18.157
what we have to do.

19:34.048 --> 19:35.883
This place is incredibly fancy.

19:36.509 --> 19:39.929
He must've made a fortune.

19:42.014 --> 19:43.974
Hey, what are you doing?

19:45.267 --> 19:46.644
Can't you tell?

19:46.727 --> 19:47.687
I'm looking around.

20:01.033 --> 20:02.910
You know, back in the day,

20:02.993 --> 20:06.038
this place used to sell things
like ointments and stomach medicine.

20:06.122 --> 20:07.581
It was just a local pharmacy.

20:08.666 --> 20:11.043
Over time,
it became a pharmaceutical company

20:12.002 --> 20:13.629
and made quite a bit of money.

20:14.255 --> 20:16.966
Enough for the owner's son
to become my client.

20:17.717 --> 20:18.884
But that should've been it.

20:19.885 --> 20:22.471
That was the limit of the wealth and fame

20:22.555 --> 20:24.598
this family could ever enjoy.

20:25.224 --> 20:29.812
Do you know how this company
became such a world-renowned corporation?

20:30.771 --> 20:33.065
Not all new drugs are the same.

20:33.149 --> 20:35.818
Some drugs are
more profitable than others.

20:36.610 --> 20:39.113
Like treatments for obesity or hair loss.

20:39.196 --> 20:41.073
Just imagine if someone developed those.

20:41.699 --> 20:43.951
So, what are you getting at?

20:45.035 --> 20:48.080
Are you asking me to just whip up
a miracle drug for you?

20:48.164 --> 20:51.876
- Do you really think that's possible?
- No, that's not it at all.

21:00.426 --> 21:02.845
Please, just take a look at this.

21:05.139 --> 21:06.223
What's this?

21:06.307 --> 21:07.183
NEW DRUGS

21:07.266 --> 21:08.642
Once this passes clinical trials,

21:08.726 --> 21:11.145
it will rake in
all the money in the world.

21:11.228 --> 21:14.815
It's a paper on a blockbuster new drug.

21:16.734 --> 21:18.861
But the thing is,

21:20.613 --> 21:23.699
our company wasn't the one

21:24.408 --> 21:25.951
that developed it.

21:26.911 --> 21:29.330
Forget all the complicated details.

21:29.872 --> 21:32.374
Just tell me what your wish is.

21:33.834 --> 21:38.172
I need to know if the clinical trials
for this drug will succeed or fail.

21:38.798 --> 21:40.549
I need to know for sure.

21:41.801 --> 21:47.306
So this chairman already knew
the new drug would be a success,

21:48.015 --> 21:50.643
and Mr. Hwang Dong-sik sold it
without having any idea.

21:51.519 --> 21:52.728
Excuse me.

21:53.437 --> 21:54.730
How can I help you?

21:55.397 --> 21:57.024
I'm here to see the chairman.

21:58.192 --> 22:00.236
- Pardon?
- What are you doing?

22:01.028 --> 22:01.904
Right.

22:03.113 --> 22:05.449
Now, look me straight in the eye.

22:08.828 --> 22:11.163
Where is the chairman right now?

22:13.374 --> 22:15.459
- Nice shot!
- Great shot!

22:15.543 --> 22:17.419
That was a powerful swing.

22:39.024 --> 22:41.193
What's with the weather all of a sudden?

22:42.152 --> 22:43.237
Hello, Mr. Chairman.

22:44.196 --> 22:45.364
Who are you?

22:46.282 --> 22:47.908
Hey, stop!

22:49.201 --> 22:51.745
What do you think you're doing?

22:51.829 --> 22:53.998
Stop this cart right now!

23:11.849 --> 23:13.017
The nine-tailed fox?

23:14.310 --> 23:17.313
What on earth is going on here?

23:17.396 --> 23:19.148
Welcome, Chairman Kim.

23:20.024 --> 23:21.191
Sit.

23:21.275 --> 23:23.444
I'm here because I have business with you.

23:29.700 --> 23:31.619
Hwang Dong-sik is dead.

23:32.286 --> 23:33.621
Hwang Dong-sik?

23:33.704 --> 23:35.039
Don't you remember him?

23:35.706 --> 23:38.000
You made a wish to me 30 years ago.

23:39.835 --> 23:41.712
Oh, him.

23:42.338 --> 23:44.840
You're not complete strangers.
At least go and pay your respects.

23:44.924 --> 23:47.343
You don't have much time left
on this earth either.

23:47.426 --> 23:49.261
Doing a good deed wouldn't hurt.

23:51.388 --> 23:52.723
Okay, I understand.

23:53.849 --> 23:55.517
How much should I give?

23:58.187 --> 24:00.856
I think something
other than money would be better.

24:00.940 --> 24:01.899
Something else?

24:02.524 --> 24:03.442
A building.

24:04.109 --> 24:06.779
I saw your company's building earlier.

24:06.862 --> 24:09.698
It's quite fancy and looks pretty nice.

24:10.866 --> 24:12.117
You don't mean

24:12.201 --> 24:15.579
our corporate headquarters, do you?

24:16.830 --> 24:18.916
You want me to give that
instead of condolence money?

24:18.999 --> 24:21.752
Why? Do you have a problem with that?

24:22.503 --> 24:27.549
Technically, your company only grew
big enough to build that building

24:28.175 --> 24:29.510
because of Hwang Dong-sik,

24:30.135 --> 24:32.346
the old man you stole that drug from.

24:32.429 --> 24:34.056
Stole?

24:34.139 --> 24:35.474
I paid

24:36.392 --> 24:39.728
a fair price for that drug, didn't I?

24:40.938 --> 24:44.274
Come on. Let's be honest, Chairman Kim.

24:44.942 --> 24:48.737
He wouldn't sell at any price,
but I made it happen for you,

24:49.279 --> 24:50.364
didn't I?

24:51.156 --> 24:52.533
Hey.

24:54.785 --> 24:56.662
Stop being so stubborn

24:56.745 --> 24:59.331
and just sell the drug or whatever.

25:04.128 --> 25:06.171
If it happens to fail,

25:06.255 --> 25:08.590
it will completely ruin you.

25:09.299 --> 25:10.426
Doesn't it make you anxious?

25:12.177 --> 25:16.140
You're enjoying the success
that old man should've had.

25:16.223 --> 25:17.933
Don't you think it's a fair amount?

25:18.017 --> 25:19.393
Except

25:19.476 --> 25:24.398
I already paid you a high enough price
when I made my wish.

25:24.481 --> 25:26.567
How can you do this to me now?

25:28.444 --> 25:29.528
Chairman Kim.

25:30.029 --> 25:33.240
Since we've maintained
a good relationship for such a long time,

25:33.866 --> 25:36.118
you must've forgotten

25:36.201 --> 25:38.245
exactly who I am

25:38.787 --> 25:41.874
and how easily I can ruin your life.

25:48.005 --> 25:51.425
Does it look like I'm here to negotiate?

25:59.141 --> 26:04.313
So, fixing the misdeeds
you committed in the past

26:04.938 --> 26:06.690
is the will of Heaven?

26:06.774 --> 26:09.860
What you just did was also part of that?

26:09.943 --> 26:11.111
That's right.

26:11.195 --> 26:12.821
I saved kids' lives

26:12.905 --> 26:15.991
and did endless community service,
but I didn't gain any spiritual power.

26:16.075 --> 26:18.786
But yesterday, we gave that old man
every penny we had,

26:19.286 --> 26:20.996
and we got an immediate response.

26:21.080 --> 26:22.456
What else could that mean?

26:22.539 --> 26:25.751
- We didn't even give him much, though.
- The amount doesn't matter.

26:25.834 --> 26:29.713
What matters is
that I gave him everything we had.

26:31.048 --> 26:32.549
But do you think that old man

26:32.633 --> 26:36.929
will really hand over a building
just because you said so?

26:37.012 --> 26:37.930
Of course.

26:38.555 --> 26:40.557
As long as he doesn't find out
I've become human,

26:40.641 --> 26:42.684
he can never disobey me.

26:43.852 --> 26:45.813
I've tamed him well.

26:47.898 --> 26:49.566
I'm sure you have.

26:50.359 --> 26:51.527
Anyway,

26:52.027 --> 26:53.904
let's just wait and see what happens.

26:55.280 --> 26:58.826
In the meantime,
can we go to the buffet again?

27:05.582 --> 27:07.251
The thing is,

27:07.793 --> 27:10.337
I'm completely broke right now.

27:10.420 --> 27:13.465
Can't we just ask that old man
for some money?

27:14.424 --> 27:17.594
You already took his building,
so that should be nothing, right?

27:18.428 --> 27:20.139
You really think that'd work?

27:20.222 --> 27:23.225
I'm trying to do good deeds
so you can become human,

27:23.308 --> 27:26.353
but you want me to shake down
a human for personal gain?

27:26.436 --> 27:27.896
I guess you're right.

27:28.939 --> 27:31.817
I'll take you to the buffet
once I make some money.

27:31.900 --> 27:33.068
Okay.

27:33.152 --> 27:35.445
In fact, I was just about to make some.

27:37.614 --> 27:39.491
Make money? You?

27:39.575 --> 27:40.701
How?

27:41.201 --> 27:42.119
You said it yourself.

27:42.202 --> 27:44.830
All I know is soccer,
and I don't have any other skills.

27:46.123 --> 27:48.834
So, that's how I'm going to make money.

27:54.381 --> 27:57.968
Hey, how badly do you think
we'll lose today?

27:58.051 --> 28:00.512
I don't know, maybe 4-0?

28:01.138 --> 28:02.931
If we're lucky, we might lose 3-0.

28:03.015 --> 28:05.017
Man, what's wrong with you guys?

28:05.100 --> 28:06.518
We could tie.

28:06.602 --> 28:08.604
Stop talking nonsense.

28:09.188 --> 28:10.981
How can we tie
against a second-division team?

28:11.064 --> 28:13.358
- Don't be ridiculous.
- Seriously, why did the coach

28:14.401 --> 28:16.695
schedule such a ridiculous practice match?

28:16.778 --> 28:18.572
This isn't even practice
with such a skill gap.

28:18.655 --> 28:20.115
Tell me about it.

28:20.199 --> 28:24.953
Getting crushed by guys like that
won't make us tougher.

28:25.037 --> 28:26.705
It'll just wear us down.

28:27.331 --> 28:28.415
Wait.

28:29.041 --> 28:30.292
Number 7 over there.

28:30.375 --> 28:31.793
Isn't that him?

28:32.544 --> 28:34.213
The former national team forward.

28:34.296 --> 28:35.923
It is him.

28:38.300 --> 28:40.969
- It's really him.
- No way!

28:41.553 --> 28:43.138
Damn it!

28:46.308 --> 28:48.060
Are you guys out of your minds?

28:48.143 --> 28:51.897
You went over to the opposing team
before the game even started,

28:51.980 --> 28:54.316
wagging your tails
like a bunch of neighborhood mutts,

28:54.399 --> 28:56.735
just to get some autographs?

28:56.818 --> 28:59.738
Coach, you're crumpling the paper.

29:04.326 --> 29:05.410
Unbelievable.

29:08.997 --> 29:10.332
Get your heads in the game.

29:11.208 --> 29:12.167
Listen up.

29:14.169 --> 29:15.963
What's our goal for this season?

29:22.177 --> 29:25.847
Damn it, it's escaping last place!

29:27.724 --> 29:29.226
Every time I go to a coaches' meeting,

29:29.309 --> 29:31.478
I'm too embarrassed to even show my face!

29:31.561 --> 29:34.564
Even if we can't get to the middle
of the fourth division,

29:34.648 --> 29:37.025
we sure as hell can't finish last!

29:38.902 --> 29:40.237
I know exactly

29:40.946 --> 29:43.198
what you're all thinking.

29:43.282 --> 29:47.077
"Gosh, this practice match
is going to be tough."

29:47.160 --> 29:50.580
"Why would he match us up
against a top second-division team?"

29:50.664 --> 29:52.416
That's what you're thinking, right?

29:53.250 --> 29:54.293
Well, let me tell you.

29:54.376 --> 29:57.838
I had a reason for choosing them.

29:59.506 --> 30:00.590
All right.

30:00.674 --> 30:03.218
Our strategy for this season

30:04.094 --> 30:04.970
is defense.

30:06.722 --> 30:08.724
I'm not asking you guys to win.

30:09.266 --> 30:10.600
Then what?

30:12.269 --> 30:13.395
Just sit back.

30:14.021 --> 30:16.148
Sit and lie down, even.

30:16.231 --> 30:18.066
You don't even have to attack.

30:18.150 --> 30:22.154
If they don't score a single goal,
then there's no way we can lose.

30:26.491 --> 30:27.743
You see?

30:28.744 --> 30:31.038
You get it now, right?

30:31.121 --> 30:34.124
It doesn't matter if they're
top of the second division.

30:34.207 --> 30:36.168
Just block them!

30:41.715 --> 30:43.592
- Block him!
- Move fast!

30:44.301 --> 30:45.510
Hurry up!

30:50.390 --> 30:51.391
Hey!

30:51.475 --> 30:52.851
It's okay.

30:52.934 --> 30:55.520
Hyeon-su, get out there!

30:59.441 --> 31:01.568
Damn it, I'm losing my mind.

31:02.569 --> 31:03.612
Jeez.

31:05.155 --> 31:07.157
We've got ten guys defending,

31:07.240 --> 31:09.284
and we're still
giving up goals left and right.

31:11.286 --> 31:14.331
You guys must be feeling generous!

31:14.414 --> 31:15.957
Very generous, damn it.

31:17.626 --> 31:19.336
Is this funny to you, you punk?

31:22.255 --> 31:23.465
What?

31:27.302 --> 31:29.596
Hey, Si-yeol.

31:36.186 --> 31:37.729
KIM GYEONG-HUN

31:37.854 --> 31:38.855
What are you doing here?

31:39.564 --> 31:40.774
And what's with the getup?

31:41.400 --> 31:44.236
Coach, you said I'm still
on the team roster, right?

31:45.445 --> 31:47.614
Well, yeah.

31:47.697 --> 31:49.032
Do you want to win?

31:49.116 --> 31:50.242
What?

31:51.201 --> 31:52.202
I mean,

31:52.285 --> 31:55.705
at this rate,
I don't know when I'll be able to return.

31:55.789 --> 31:58.917
But I need to stay in shape,
so I might as well play anywhere.

31:59.543 --> 32:00.919
So, I'll play for you.

32:04.256 --> 32:06.842
What are you even saying, you punk?

32:06.925 --> 32:08.844
You're out of your mind.

32:09.886 --> 32:13.140
You said your wish was promotion.

32:14.391 --> 32:16.935
I'll make sure you move up

32:18.311 --> 32:19.604
to the third division.

32:20.730 --> 32:24.776
WISHING FOR DAEHEUNG CITIZENS FC'S VICTORY

32:25.569 --> 32:27.737
There's nobody here.

32:30.490 --> 32:31.450
I know, right?

32:32.617 --> 32:35.370
Why are they even playing
when no one is watching?

32:36.037 --> 32:37.330
Such a waste of energy.

32:43.128 --> 32:45.589
Anyway, where is Si-yeol?

32:48.884 --> 32:51.887
- Kang Si-yeol, let's go!
- Si-yeol, you can do it!

32:51.970 --> 32:53.138
Let's go, Si-yeol!

32:53.221 --> 32:54.347
Stay focused!

32:54.431 --> 32:56.141
Si-yeol's here.

33:07.652 --> 33:10.322
- Over here.
- Why pass it now?

33:35.639 --> 33:38.183
Hey, look at the score! We're losing!

33:38.266 --> 33:39.768
Come here, let me give you a kiss!

33:39.851 --> 33:41.394
Hurry and get back in position!

33:41.478 --> 33:42.771
But didn't you say

33:43.438 --> 33:46.691
they're doing well
if they put the ball in there?

33:46.775 --> 33:48.985
Why is Si-yeol so angry?

33:52.906 --> 33:54.658
Because he has a bad temper.

33:59.621 --> 34:02.290
INTENSIVE CARE UNIT

34:19.391 --> 34:20.850
I'm sure you know

34:20.934 --> 34:24.271
that your body is falling apart.

34:28.483 --> 34:29.734
When that day comes,

34:30.569 --> 34:32.445
all the spirits you've devoured

34:32.529 --> 34:37.242
will tear your soul to pieces.

34:37.325 --> 34:39.411
They'll slash, tear, and crush you.

34:39.494 --> 34:44.165
They'll chew you up and spit you out.

34:44.791 --> 34:48.587
Unable to die, yet unable to live.

34:49.296 --> 34:51.256
That's the fate that awaits you.

35:19.326 --> 35:20.327
Hey!

35:22.704 --> 35:26.750
Man, you've become
quite pathetic yourself.

35:28.084 --> 35:29.878
I'd heard you were close to death,

35:29.961 --> 35:32.505
but look at you,
coughing up blood and collapsing.

35:37.177 --> 35:39.512
This hospital belongs to our foundation.

35:39.596 --> 35:41.931
I told them to look out for you
just in case,

35:42.015 --> 35:43.350
and they notified me right away.

35:43.433 --> 35:45.769
I've been looking for you,

35:45.852 --> 35:48.772
but I had no way of contacting you.

35:49.689 --> 35:50.815
Why were you looking for me?

35:52.442 --> 35:54.361
There's someone I'd like you to meet.

35:59.115 --> 36:00.116
That's it.

36:00.909 --> 36:04.120
What on earth is happening right now?

36:04.204 --> 36:05.455
I don't know.

36:05.997 --> 36:07.999
Is this score for real?

36:08.541 --> 36:10.710
How many minutes has it been
since Si-yeol went in?

36:10.794 --> 36:12.754
It's been about 13 minutes.

36:12.837 --> 36:14.923
Gosh, that hat trick.

36:15.006 --> 36:16.800
He's totally insane!

36:28.561 --> 36:30.271
- Nice.
- Yes!

36:30.897 --> 36:32.816
Hey! What are you guys doing?

36:32.899 --> 36:35.110
Aren't you going to block Number 10?

36:35.193 --> 36:37.195
That guy's going to lose his voice soon.

36:39.989 --> 36:41.032
Hey, Ref!

36:41.116 --> 36:42.742
That's a foul.

36:42.826 --> 36:46.037
Are you blind? Watch the damn game!

36:51.000 --> 36:52.669
Ref!

36:52.752 --> 36:55.630
You, Ref! Do your job!

36:58.591 --> 37:01.094
I've got the whole defense on me.

37:01.177 --> 37:03.138
How are those idiots not scoring?

37:04.264 --> 37:05.765
Unbelievable.

37:05.849 --> 37:07.976
I haven't even run that much.

37:08.059 --> 37:10.812
How out of shape am I?
I'm already worn out.

37:11.396 --> 37:13.227
Si-yeol!

37:22.490 --> 37:23.700
Damn it!

37:27.036 --> 37:28.413
I can't keep going like this.

37:31.833 --> 37:33.042
Hey, Si-yeol!

37:33.585 --> 37:36.379
Get a grip. You're losing!

37:36.463 --> 37:40.008
Man, that temper of hers.

37:40.091 --> 37:42.260
I'll never hear the end of it if we lose.

37:50.143 --> 37:54.189
- How much time do we have left?
- They gave three minutes of added time.

37:54.272 --> 37:57.025
I think this is the last chance to score.

37:57.108 --> 37:58.401
Really?

37:58.485 --> 37:59.611
Damn it.

38:00.320 --> 38:03.990
All I'm asking for is just one more goal.

38:13.666 --> 38:14.834
That was a total foul!

38:14.918 --> 38:16.961
- Penalty kick!
- Penalty kick!

38:17.045 --> 38:19.088
That's a penalty. You have to call it.

38:19.172 --> 38:20.882
Ref!

38:20.965 --> 38:24.844
- Yes!
- We got a penalty kick!

38:24.928 --> 38:26.221
Penalty kick!

38:33.645 --> 38:35.605
KANG SI-YEOL

38:41.736 --> 38:43.822
Stay calm. Don't cheer. Don't get nervous.

38:44.447 --> 38:46.574
Here he goes. Please…

38:52.664 --> 38:54.082
Kang Si-yeol!

39:14.185 --> 39:17.021
That's our Kang Si-yeol!

39:17.105 --> 39:20.775
I knew you could do it!
Why didn't you play like this before?

39:22.402 --> 39:23.945
Don't.

39:25.363 --> 39:26.823
What's with the mood in here?

39:27.574 --> 39:28.992
Coach, hold on a second.

39:29.617 --> 39:32.203
Seo Beom, what the hell was that earlier?

39:32.287 --> 39:33.246
Me?

39:33.329 --> 39:35.665
Who makes that pass at that moment?

39:35.748 --> 39:37.333
You should've waited.

39:37.417 --> 39:40.253
Draw the defense in first,
then make the pass!

39:41.504 --> 39:42.463
And you!

39:42.547 --> 39:43.548
Bae Jeong-bae, right?

39:43.631 --> 39:46.885
Why didn't you take the chance
to cut inside when you had it?

39:46.968 --> 39:50.138
When I drew the defense out to the side,

39:50.221 --> 39:53.141
you should've exploited the space!

39:53.224 --> 39:54.434
Unbelievable!

39:56.853 --> 39:58.646
Did I misread the score?

39:58.730 --> 40:00.565
Did we lose?

40:00.648 --> 40:01.691
No, we tied.

40:02.317 --> 40:03.526
We did, right?

40:04.444 --> 40:05.987
Then why does it feel like we lost?

40:06.070 --> 40:09.324
Tell me about it. You'd think we lost.

40:09.824 --> 40:11.326
We didn't win!

40:11.868 --> 40:15.538
Where's the fight? Where's the hunger?

40:15.622 --> 40:17.457
You're all just slacking off.

40:18.082 --> 40:19.709
Don't you guys want to win?

40:20.251 --> 40:21.544
Are you okay with losing?

40:22.170 --> 40:23.254
Gosh.

40:23.922 --> 40:26.466
I'm going to step out for a second.

40:27.258 --> 40:29.344
Coach! Where are you going?

40:29.427 --> 40:30.929
- Well--
- You can't leave.

40:31.012 --> 40:32.180
Explain this to me, Coach.

40:32.263 --> 40:34.641
With 13 minutes left, 4-0?

40:34.724 --> 40:37.101
And how are you guys excited about this?

40:37.185 --> 40:38.478
You!

40:38.561 --> 40:41.773
Look at the size of you.
How are you so bad at defending?

40:43.566 --> 40:45.944
Si-yeol was absolutely incredible today.

40:46.027 --> 40:46.903
Don't you think so?

40:48.655 --> 40:51.282
Well, that's the bare minimum.

40:51.366 --> 40:53.326
He is a pro soccer player, after all.

40:53.409 --> 40:57.121
I don't know why everyone's making
such a big deal over a few goals.

41:01.542 --> 41:02.543
Bang!

41:08.925 --> 41:11.552
Anyway, aren't you leaving?
How long are you staying?

41:13.221 --> 41:14.472
Beat it!

41:21.104 --> 41:23.022
Man, I'm really late.

41:23.898 --> 41:25.900
I'm heading out first, guys.

41:25.984 --> 41:27.485
- Good game!
- Catch you later!

41:32.073 --> 41:32.991
Hey.

41:34.575 --> 41:36.285
Did you pay Gyeong-hun back?

41:36.369 --> 41:37.745
Money? What for?

41:38.496 --> 41:41.207
You abandoned his car
on some back road in Gyeonggi Province.

41:41.290 --> 41:42.709
He said the towing fees were huge.

41:42.792 --> 41:44.002
Didn't he mention it?

41:44.627 --> 41:47.380
Oh, I didn't even think of that.

41:48.548 --> 41:49.424
I'll pay him back.

41:50.133 --> 41:52.510
Tell him to sit tight
now that I'm back on the field.

41:52.593 --> 41:54.095
I'll have the cash in no time.

41:54.178 --> 41:56.014
While we're on the subject,

41:56.097 --> 41:57.765
how much am I worth again?

41:58.266 --> 42:00.435
Why am I so broke right now?

42:01.644 --> 42:03.688
Did you just ask
what the payout is if you die?

42:03.771 --> 42:06.566
Did you take out a life insurance policy?

42:07.066 --> 42:08.484
No, my paycheck.

42:08.568 --> 42:10.653
How much do I make a week?

42:10.737 --> 42:12.989
- What?
- Weekly pay?

42:13.072 --> 42:16.367
It's the fourth division,
so it won't be much.

42:16.868 --> 42:18.953
Do I make about two or three million won?

42:19.037 --> 42:21.289
Are you crazy?

42:21.372 --> 42:24.042
Even less? One million, then?

42:24.125 --> 42:25.960
A million won a week?

42:26.044 --> 42:28.921
Who do you think you are, a pro?

42:29.005 --> 42:31.049
You've never earned a weekly wage.

42:31.132 --> 42:32.175
It's not a weekly wage?

42:33.009 --> 42:34.886
I guess they pay
an annual salary in Korea.

42:35.762 --> 42:38.139
I mean, it's not like
I've ever played in the K League.

42:38.222 --> 42:41.184
You're not on an annual salary.
You get paid per game.

42:42.935 --> 42:44.562
- Per game?
- Yes.

42:45.438 --> 42:48.733
It's 50,000 won per game,
and 300,000 for a win.

42:48.816 --> 42:50.359
What are you talking about?

42:51.277 --> 42:52.487
That's it?

42:53.863 --> 42:55.031
What about a base salary?

42:55.114 --> 42:58.159
There isn't any.
Our team doesn't even pay for training.

42:58.242 --> 43:01.829
Actually, compared
to other fourth-division teams,

43:01.913 --> 43:03.498
we're in pretty bad shape

43:03.998 --> 43:05.666
since we're always in last place.

43:07.543 --> 43:11.047
So you're saying
if there are four games a month,

43:11.130 --> 43:13.091
that's 350,000 won times four.

43:16.010 --> 43:18.221
Only 1.4 million won?

43:18.805 --> 43:20.264
Your math is way off.

43:20.348 --> 43:22.558
We can't win every game.
We lose almost all of them.

43:23.518 --> 43:26.479
It's 50,000 won times four,
so it's 200,000 won.

43:27.105 --> 43:28.064
Hey.

43:28.147 --> 43:30.942
You at least get that 200,000 won
because you're a starter.

43:31.025 --> 43:32.985
Look at Gyeong-hun.
He's just a backup goalie.

43:33.069 --> 43:36.239
When was the last time he played?
Was it last year?

43:36.322 --> 43:37.198
Yeah.

43:37.281 --> 43:39.117
Then how much does he get paid?

43:39.200 --> 43:40.660
Nothing.

43:40.743 --> 43:43.412
He trains like crazy,
but he doesn't get paid at all.

43:43.496 --> 43:46.040
That's why he's out
doing delivery gigs day and night.

43:46.124 --> 43:48.584
Do you get it now?
You ripped off a poor kid like that.

43:50.461 --> 43:52.380
Then how do you guys survive?

43:53.005 --> 43:54.966
You can't live on 200,000 won a month.

43:55.049 --> 43:56.592
We all have part-time jobs.

43:57.135 --> 43:58.219
Except for Jeong-bae.

44:00.888 --> 44:03.099
Forget about the sports car guy.

44:03.182 --> 44:06.811
So you guys have jobs
other than playing soccer?

44:07.436 --> 44:09.355
Then how can you focus on training?

44:09.438 --> 44:11.691
So stop giving them such a hard time.

44:11.774 --> 44:14.152
They're all just
trying their best to get by.

44:16.654 --> 44:17.613
I'm heading out.

44:18.156 --> 44:20.324
- See you tomorrow.
- Take care.

44:38.843 --> 44:39.760
Hey!

44:40.344 --> 44:42.972
What took you so long?
I've been waiting forever.

44:43.055 --> 44:44.098
Oh, sorry.

44:45.057 --> 44:46.434
But why are you alone?

44:48.686 --> 44:49.729
She left.

44:50.771 --> 44:51.898
I see.

44:55.651 --> 44:57.820
What's going on with you?

44:58.446 --> 44:59.405
What?

44:59.488 --> 45:04.368
I mean, you played pretty well today,
but you look so dejected.

45:05.745 --> 45:08.456
Did that Coach Park give you a hard time?

45:10.374 --> 45:11.542
It's not that.

45:13.920 --> 45:17.506
I've just got some stuff on my mind.

45:18.132 --> 45:19.550
And most of all,

45:19.634 --> 45:21.594
I didn't make any money.

45:22.678 --> 45:25.598
Even if it was a practice game,
I thought I'd at least get paid.

45:25.681 --> 45:27.725
So it was about money?

45:28.351 --> 45:29.227
Don't worry about it.

45:29.310 --> 45:31.646
I can just make that money myself.

45:31.729 --> 45:32.647
Besides,

45:33.856 --> 45:35.983
you looked pretty cool out there today.

45:39.111 --> 45:42.281
Right, like you're going to make money.

45:42.365 --> 45:45.159
Wait, then what do we do
about our date tonight?

45:45.826 --> 45:47.411
- What?
- Don't you remember?

45:47.495 --> 45:50.039
We couldn't have one last night
because it was too hectic,

45:50.122 --> 45:52.333
so we agreed to go on our date tonight.

45:53.960 --> 45:56.337
Are we postponing it again?

45:57.964 --> 46:00.800
Well, we can just go some other time.

46:00.883 --> 46:02.718
What's the rush?

46:02.802 --> 46:04.679
You said it was just
a hobby for you anyway.

46:05.930 --> 46:09.809
Damn, we should've kept some cash
instead of giving it all away.

46:10.393 --> 46:12.853
Man, where can I get some money?

46:13.354 --> 46:15.398
Hey, Si-yeol!

46:15.481 --> 46:16.482
And your girlfriend!

46:20.152 --> 46:22.196
Why are you guys still here?

46:22.280 --> 46:23.489
Si-yeol.

46:23.572 --> 46:26.617
Isn't that the guy who was
driving that fancy sports car?

46:26.701 --> 46:27.702
Yeah.

46:28.786 --> 46:33.457
I heard his family owns
a famous galbi restaurant in Seoul.

47:17.585 --> 47:18.669
What are you staring at?

47:19.420 --> 47:21.422
- Do I look weird?
- What?

47:22.381 --> 47:24.467
No, of course not.

47:24.550 --> 47:26.010
It's just that…

47:29.722 --> 47:34.226
I guess expensive clothes
really do make you look good.

47:35.686 --> 47:36.771
Right?

47:36.854 --> 47:41.400
I need to get back to my old self
and buy this in every color.

47:44.236 --> 47:47.531
Anyway, where are we going?

47:48.407 --> 47:49.742
Do you have a plan?

47:50.701 --> 47:52.453
A plan?

47:55.206 --> 47:58.125
I just thought of something.

47:59.085 --> 48:00.961
- What is it?
- Namsan.

48:01.629 --> 48:03.631
Namsan is the ultimate
date spot, after all.

48:13.557 --> 48:17.436
Jeez, you've been going on about a date
since yesterday morning,

48:17.520 --> 48:19.980
so I was wondering
what kind of grand plans you had in mind.

48:20.064 --> 48:21.941
Was Namsan all you could come up with?

48:23.192 --> 48:24.652
How cliché.

48:25.528 --> 48:27.405
I'm not looking for anything
out of the ordinary.

48:27.488 --> 48:29.407
I want a totally cliché, classic romance.

48:29.490 --> 48:31.867
And where else would we go but here?

48:33.619 --> 48:37.248
Well, when you put it that way,
I guess you have a point.

48:39.583 --> 48:43.671
Since you're human now,
it's time to do everything you wanted.

48:48.134 --> 48:50.719
That! I've always wanted to try that.

48:50.803 --> 48:53.347
It's a classic, right? Let's go.

48:59.812 --> 49:04.024
So we just write our wish on this, right?

49:04.608 --> 49:05.651
That's about it.

49:13.325 --> 49:14.452
MAY OUR LOVE LAST FOREVER

49:15.536 --> 49:16.745
LET'S COME BACK IN TEN YEARS!

49:24.920 --> 49:26.297
Wait, what's this?

49:26.380 --> 49:28.716
I thought you wanted something classic.

49:29.258 --> 49:31.010
EUN-HO, KANG SI-YEOL
BACK TO HOW WE WERE

49:31.760 --> 49:34.388
This is a wish. I have to be realistic.

49:35.097 --> 49:37.933
What other wish
could possibly be more important?

49:38.017 --> 49:39.935
I'm just saying.

49:40.019 --> 49:43.230
Did you have to bring us
back to reality on this?

49:45.107 --> 49:48.068
Are you pouting
because my wish wasn't romantic enough?

49:48.736 --> 49:50.654
Who's pouting?

49:50.738 --> 49:51.739
Don't be ridiculous.

49:51.822 --> 49:53.657
I'm just playing along for your sake.

49:53.741 --> 49:54.909
Why would I be pouting?

49:54.992 --> 49:58.329
Fine, I'll just do something
more classic, then.

50:01.415 --> 50:03.292
Is this better?

50:03.375 --> 50:05.503
What are you doing?

50:05.586 --> 50:07.296
A heart between us?

50:07.379 --> 50:09.298
You said a wish has to be realistic.

50:09.381 --> 50:11.050
What if this jinxes it?

50:11.133 --> 50:13.594
You worry too much.

50:13.677 --> 50:16.388
Once things are back to normal,
we'll go our separate ways.

50:16.472 --> 50:17.765
This heart doesn't mean anything.

50:17.848 --> 50:20.643
This heart won't matter at all by then.

50:20.726 --> 50:22.561
Hey, you didn't have to go that far.

50:22.645 --> 50:24.897
Whatever. Let's just hang this here.

50:24.980 --> 50:26.315
Goodness.

50:26.815 --> 50:28.859
Hang it or don't. I don't care.

50:28.943 --> 50:30.069
There.

50:49.088 --> 50:50.673
Dad, I'm home.

51:06.021 --> 51:08.065
Do we have a guest?

51:09.567 --> 51:12.111
Oh, you're home?

51:14.446 --> 51:15.614
What are you doing here?

51:16.240 --> 51:17.700
How did you get in here?

51:20.911 --> 51:22.288
Where's my dad?

51:23.372 --> 51:24.707
He's just over there.

51:27.751 --> 51:28.836
Dad!

51:31.630 --> 51:32.756
Dad.

51:34.091 --> 51:36.135
Wake up!

51:42.933 --> 51:46.228
What did you do to my father?

51:47.896 --> 51:51.567
He's just unconscious,
that's all.

51:51.650 --> 51:53.110
Man, I feel refreshed.

51:54.194 --> 51:57.156
Even the shower's amazing
in a fancy house.

52:02.244 --> 52:04.038
Answer me!

52:05.247 --> 52:08.125
What did you do to him?

52:08.208 --> 52:10.085
There's no need to worry.

52:10.169 --> 52:13.505
He'll be fine
once he wakes up from his little nap.

52:14.048 --> 52:16.467
By the way, I heard you lost your memory.

52:17.134 --> 52:18.427
I told you

52:18.510 --> 52:21.972
I knew someone
who can help with this kind of thing.

52:22.056 --> 52:25.351
Meet Jang Do-cheol. He's a shaman.

52:26.477 --> 52:27.728
A male shaman.

52:27.811 --> 52:28.896
A shaman?

52:29.521 --> 52:32.733
What, did you expect me to bring a priest?

52:33.317 --> 52:37.446
All you want is
to get your memory back, right?

52:39.823 --> 52:42.451
I said we should eat something nice
since we're out anyway.

52:42.534 --> 52:44.244
What's wrong with pork cutlet?

52:44.745 --> 52:46.413
Isn't it totally a classic?

52:46.497 --> 52:49.833
Besides, how much were you planning
to spend on borrowed money?

52:57.424 --> 52:58.342
Here.

53:00.010 --> 53:01.845
Look at you being so cooperative.

53:02.471 --> 53:04.473
It's just manners.

53:04.556 --> 53:05.974
It's second nature to me.

53:07.101 --> 53:09.812
Still, I like it. It's also classic.

53:18.112 --> 53:19.571
Si-yeol,

53:20.364 --> 53:22.783
isn't there anything
you've wanted to do on a date?

53:24.034 --> 53:25.369
I don't know.

53:26.745 --> 53:28.706
I just wanted something normal too.

53:28.789 --> 53:30.958
Not having to date inside a car

53:31.625 --> 53:32.793
or hide my face.

53:33.460 --> 53:36.714
Something like holding hands
and walking down a crowded street.

53:37.256 --> 53:38.674
I've never done that before.

53:39.925 --> 53:40.843
Really?

53:42.094 --> 53:45.472
I was hoping for some fun ideas,
but that's it?

53:47.057 --> 53:50.436
Living as a celebrity must be exhausting.

53:51.061 --> 53:53.981
I can just do whatever I want
and erase people's memories.

54:06.201 --> 54:07.828
Erase that human's memory.

54:08.537 --> 54:09.913
Erase it.

54:11.206 --> 54:13.250
Sis, I found a way!

54:13.792 --> 54:16.295
I found a way for you to turn back

54:16.378 --> 54:17.755
into a nine-tailed fox.

54:23.343 --> 54:26.263
How about it? Do you remember now?

54:30.601 --> 54:31.477
Tell us.

54:31.560 --> 54:33.520
What do you know?

54:33.604 --> 54:34.605
Well…

54:38.066 --> 54:39.359
She said she became human.

54:40.611 --> 54:41.945
What?

54:43.947 --> 54:45.365
That nine-tailed fox.

54:46.283 --> 54:49.119
She's just an ordinary human now.

54:54.374 --> 54:56.043
Si-yeol, hold my hand.

54:57.252 --> 54:58.212
What?

54:58.712 --> 55:00.506
This was the date you wanted to go on.

55:00.589 --> 55:02.800
We're on a date,
so let's hold hands as we walk.

55:04.134 --> 55:05.677
Oh, come on.

55:06.345 --> 55:08.847
Seriously, how long
are you going to keep this up?

55:19.316 --> 55:20.901
You know, it's strange.

55:21.401 --> 55:22.277
What is?

55:22.361 --> 55:23.612
I mean, until just recently,

55:23.695 --> 55:26.907
my heart would race,
and I'd get nervous around you.

55:26.990 --> 55:30.577
But now
that we're actually dating like this,

55:30.661 --> 55:31.954
my heart doesn't race anymore,

55:32.037 --> 55:35.749
even when we're holding hands
or I'm lying on your arm.

55:35.833 --> 55:38.836
Is something wrong with our relationship?

55:40.712 --> 55:44.424
Are you saying this doesn't
make your heart race at all?

55:45.300 --> 55:46.426
Not at all.

55:49.596 --> 55:51.557
Are you toying with me?

55:53.392 --> 55:55.936
But I actually had fun on our date today.

55:56.019 --> 55:59.648
I think I'll remember it for a long time
because it was so ordinary and classic.

56:02.317 --> 56:06.029
Speaking of memories,

56:07.739 --> 56:11.326
when things go back to normal,
are you going to erase my memory too?

56:12.452 --> 56:13.912
What?

56:13.996 --> 56:15.789
You just said earlier

56:15.873 --> 56:19.877
that you'd do what you want
and then erase the memory.

56:21.545 --> 56:25.924
I mean, I ended up
learning too much about you.

56:26.758 --> 56:30.596
So, like you did to Woo-seok
and that old man,

56:31.221 --> 56:33.223
I wondered if you'd just erase mine too.

56:34.516 --> 56:36.351
Why would you suddenly ask that?

56:37.060 --> 56:39.062
Because of what you said

56:39.146 --> 56:42.232
about going our separate ways
once everything is back to normal.

56:42.316 --> 56:43.942
I'm going to erase it.

56:44.026 --> 56:46.862
To me, human friends
have always been disposable.

56:47.779 --> 56:51.116
I have my fun,
and then I wipe the slate clean.

56:51.199 --> 56:54.620
That way,
things don't get emotionally messy.

56:54.703 --> 56:55.579
It's cleaner that way.

56:58.290 --> 57:02.419
Hearing that makes me feel a bit sad.

57:05.130 --> 57:06.256
It doesn't make you sad?

57:08.800 --> 57:09.801
It does.

57:14.264 --> 57:17.726
It's obvious that I'm special to you,

57:17.809 --> 57:19.186
but to me, you're also…

57:20.562 --> 57:22.189
a pretty special human.

57:23.065 --> 57:28.320
You're the first human friend I've had
who didn't feel disposable.

57:28.946 --> 57:31.865
Of course it'll be sad
after I erase your memory.

57:32.824 --> 57:34.451
Then don't erase it.

57:35.911 --> 57:37.037
I can't.

57:37.120 --> 57:38.455
Why not?

57:38.538 --> 57:41.708
Because then your life won't be normal.

57:41.792 --> 57:43.835
For a human to live a normal life,

57:43.919 --> 57:46.338
memories of switched fates
and a nine-tailed fox becoming human

57:46.421 --> 57:47.965
are better forgotten.

57:48.799 --> 57:51.134
So, erasing your memory

57:52.260 --> 57:54.179
is my final gift to you.

58:00.060 --> 58:01.520
What if…

58:04.606 --> 58:06.358
I don't want to be normal?

58:08.402 --> 58:09.277
What?

58:09.903 --> 58:12.239
If you're just going to erase my memory

58:12.990 --> 58:15.367
and be the only one
who remembers this moment…

58:18.203 --> 58:21.832
then I should be allowed to do
at least this much, right?

58:23.000 --> 58:24.292
What do you mean…

58:55.532 --> 58:57.492
SPECIAL APPEARANCES
BY KIM HONG-PA AND OH MIN-SEOK

59:18.930 --> 59:21.600
EUN-HO, KANG SI-YEOL
BACK TO HOW WE WERE

59:21.683 --> 59:24.603
NO TAIL TO TELL

59:24.686 --> 59:27.064
Let's date. For real.

59:27.147 --> 59:29.858
Don't think about running.
Let's do this right.

59:31.359 --> 59:34.362
Eun-ho, should we go on a trip?

59:34.446 --> 59:36.907
Then who erased your memory?

59:36.990 --> 59:38.784
There was someone else there.

59:38.867 --> 59:41.912
He told me to wait and do nothing,
but what the hell is he doing?

59:41.995 --> 59:43.747
Here. I made some money.

59:43.830 --> 59:45.619
Wait, what did you do to get…

59:46.166 --> 59:48.376
I'm on a mission
to do good deeds right now.

59:48.460 --> 59:50.253
Hey, Si-yeol!

59:50.879 --> 59:52.089
Hyeon Woo-seok collapsed!

59:52.172 --> 59:54.007
- Woo-seok!
- Hey, Woo-seok!

59:54.091 --> 59:56.009
They say he might die.

59:59.513 --> 01:00:01.515
Subtitle translation by Susanna Kim
